    "https://oulunyliopisto.varbi.com/en/what:job/jobID:798680/": {
      "title": "Doctoral Researcher in health sciences",
      "description": "Doctoral Researcher in health sciences Login and apply Swedish Norwegian Danish Finnish German Dutch Chinese (BETA) Polish French Romanian Norwegian (nynorsk) Doctoral Researcher in health sciences Login and apply Faculty of Medicine, Health Sciences and Technology The University of Oulu is a multidisciplinary, international research university, with about 4000 employees who produce new knowledge based on high-standards research and provide research based education to build a more sustainable, smarter, and more humane world. The University of Oulu community has about 19,000 people in total. Our northern scientific community operates globally and creates conditions for the emergence of innovations. The University of Oulu is ranked in the top 3% of the world’s universities. All our research, education, and community activities are guided by our university’s values and ethical principles. We are now looking for a Doctoral Researcher to join the HealthEduCom Lab in the Research Unit of Health Sciences and Technology (HST), Faculty of Medicine, University of Oulu. The HealthEduCom Lab conducts multidisciplinary research on healthcare education, learning environments, mentoring and educator competence, predictive models of professional learning, and hybrid intelligence in extended reality (XR) contexts. The lab brings together expertise in health sciences, pedagogy, technology-enhanced learning and human-AI collaboration. You will work in an international research environment with access to the University of Oulu's Hybrid Intelligence research profile, the LEAF research infrastructure, and OuluHealth Labs in collaboration with the Wellbeing Services County of North Ostrobothnia. About the project The position is part of the Playful Entrepreneurial Minds: Playfulness and Hybrid Intelligence in Higher Education and Working Life (Playful Minds) project funded by the Research Council of Finland. The consortium brings together the University of Lapland, the University of Oulu and the University of Turku, together with national and international research and working-life partners. At the University of Oulu, we focus on hybrid intelligence, multirealities and playful learning in healthcare and medical education. Its overarching aim is to develop, implement, and validate a multidimensional Hybrid Intelligence-Playful Learning (HI-PL) framework that integrates playfulness, an entrepreneurial mindset, and hybrid intelligence into XR-based healthcare learning. The research uses a design-based research approach and combines qualitative, quantitative, behavioural and physiological data. About the job As a Doctoral Researcher, you will: Conduct doctoral research on hybrid intelligence-enabled playful learning in healthcare and medical education and complete a doctoral degree during the four-year employment period. Contribute to the co-design, implementation and validation of the HI-PL framework in nursing, health sciences and healthcare practice contexts. Plan and facilitate participatory workshops and pilot sessions with higher education students, academic professionals and healthcare professionals. Design and conduct controlled XR-based simulation studies involving playful human-AI interaction, metacognitive reflection, clinical decision-making and adaptive performance in demanding clinical scenarios. Collect and analyse multimodal research data, including questionnaires on playfulness, psychological safety, wellbeing, metacognition and engagement; behavioural and performance data from XR sessions and video recordings; and physiological indicators such as heart rate variability. Conduct interviews, focus groups and analyses of reflective learning logs to evaluate learning experiences, psychological safety, meaningful engagement and the usability of the HI-PL framework. Use design-based research and suitable qualitative, quantitative and mixed-method approaches to iteratively refine the framework and develop implementation guidance for healthcare curricula. Contribute to ethical review applications, research permissions, responsible data management, open science and GDPR-compliant research practices. Collaborate across the Playful Minds consortium and with national and international partners, including researchers in health sciences, education, learning sciences, technology and entrepreneurship. Complete doctoral studies at the University of Oulu Graduate School and publish the findings in high-quality international peer-reviewed journals and conferences. You will receive regular supervision and multidisciplinary support while gradually taking responsibility for your research questions, methodological choices, publications and international research profile. You will receive regular supervision and multidisciplinary support while gradually taking responsibility for your research questions, methodological choices, publications and international research profile. What we offer? A four-year, full-time Doctoral Researcher position in an ambitious multidisciplinary project addressing learning, wellbeing and professional competence in the era of hybrid intelligence. The support of the experienced and enthusiastic HealthEduCom Lab and the wider Playful Minds consortium, where you can share your expertise and grow as an independent researcher. Access to expertise in healthcare education, playful learning, hybrid intelligence, XR-based simulation, learning analytics, physiological measurement and mixed-method research. Access to relevant research infrastructure and authentic learning environments, including LEAF and OuluHealth Labs, subject to the final research protocols and permissions. Opportunities for national and international collaboration, conference participation, co-authored publications and research mobility when relevant to your doctoral project. Wellness benefit ePassi covering sport, culture and well-being. Read more about other staff benefits. Development and career options of the big organization. Work that matters and a workplace that promotes flexibility and work-life balance. Read more about working with us . Our Buddy Programme and Spouse Network support you and close ones in settling into Oulu. We have an HR Excellence in Research -quality label which is a recognition awarded by the European Commission for the development of researchers’ working conditions and careers. Finland is one of the most livable countries in the world, with a high quality of life, safety, an excellent education system, and a competitive economy. Read more about living in Oulu . Who are you? In order to succeed and enjoy the position, we expect from you: A relevant Master's degree in health sciences / nursing science / health pedagogy. The degree must be completed before the employment begins . Eligibility to pursue doctoral studies and willingness to apply for doctoral study rights at the University of Oulu Graduate School at the beginning of the employment, unless you already hold the relevant study right. A strong motivation to conduct long-term doctoral research at the intersection of healthcare education, human-AI collaboration, playful learning and XR-based simulation. Foundational competence in research methods and readiness to develop expertise in qualitative, quantitative and mixed-method research. Ability to plan and carry out research responsibly, systematically and independently while working constructively in a multidisciplinary and international team. Good communication, collaboration and academic writing skills. Fluent written and spoken English. See also the requirements of the University of Oulu Graduate School (UniOGS) Experience in one or more of the following areas will be considered an advantage: Healthcare education, nursing or medical education, clinical practice, simulation-based education, or professional competence development. Hybrid intelligence, artificial intelligence in education, human-AI interaction, XR or other multireality learning environments. Design-based research, co-design, participatory research, intervention studies or experimental research. Qualitative methods such as interviews, focus groups, observations, content analysis or thematic analysis. Quantitative and mixed-method research, including questionnaire studies, multilevel modelling, structural equation modelling or correlation analysis. Collection or analysis of behavioural, video or physiological data, including heart rate variability. Relevant research software, for example R, SPSS, Stata, Mplus, NVivo or comparable tools. Research publications, conference presentations, open-science activities or previous work in a research project. Finnish language skills, especially for collaboration and data collection in Finnish healthcare and higher education contexts. Salary The position is fixed-term for four years as of 1.10.2026 or as soon as possible thereafter. The salary will be based on the levels 2-4 of the demand level chart for teaching and research staff of Finnish universities. In addition, a salary component based on personal work performance will be paid (a maximum of 50 % of the job-specific component). The starting gross salary will be approx. 2500-3200 € per month (before taxes).  A trial period of 6 months is applied in the position. How to apply? Interested? If yes, please apply by 13.9.2026 (23:59 Finnish local time) through our recruitment system. The application should be written in English and include the following: Cover letter CV following the guidelines of the Finnish Advisory Board on Research Integrity Research plan , maximum three pages plus references. Describe a feasible doctoral study aligned with the aims of a project. The final doctoral research plan will be refined together with the supervisors. List of publications , if applicable. Use a clear and standard academic format. The eligible applicants fitting best in the profile expected for the position will be invited to an on-site or remote interview. All applicants will be notified during the selection process. We welcome applicants from all backgrounds, such as people of different ages, genders, and lingual, cultural, or minority groups. Contact Information If you have any further questions, please contact Docent Heli Kuivila Research Unit of Health Sciences and Technology, Faculty of Medicine, University of Oulu Email: Heli-Maria.Kuivila@oulu.fi | Tel.: +358294485609 Professor Kristina Mikkonen Research Unit of Health Sciences and Technology, Faculty of Medicine, University of Oulu Email: kristina.mikkonen@oulu.fi | Tel.: +358 505754686 Type of employment Temporary position over 6 months Contract type Full time Number of positions 1 Full-time equivalent 100 % City Oulu County Pohjois-Pohjanmaa Country Finland Reference number 2025/138 Published 14.Aug.2026 Last application date 13.Sep.2026 Login and apply Share links Return to job vacancies Grade Varbi Recruit recruitment system Cookies Terms Data privacy policy Accessibility statement × Modal title We use cookies for login, improved user experience, share links and in some cases marketing and collection of statistics. Accept all cookies Accept only necessary Read more about our cookies here ×"
    },
    "https://oulunyliopisto.varbi.com/en/what:job/jobID:957102/": {
      "title": "Postdoctoral Researcher, Geography, Faculty of Science",
      "description": "Postdoctoral Researcher, Geography, Faculty of Science Login and apply Swedish Norwegian Danish Finnish German Dutch Chinese (BETA) Polish French Romanian Norwegian (nynorsk) Postdoctoral Researcher, Geography, Faculty of Science Login and apply Faculty of Science, Geography The University of Oulu is a multidisciplinary, international research university, with about 4000 employees who produce new knowledge based on high-standards research and provide research based education to build a more sustainable, smarter, and more humane world. The University of Oulu community has about 19,000 people in total. Our northern scientific community operates globally and creates conditions for the emergence of innovations. The University of Oulu is ranked in the top 3% of the world’s universities. All our research, education, and community activities are guided by our university’s values and ethical principles. We are now looking for a Postdoctoral Researcher to work in a two (2) year fixed-term position with our talented freshwater plant research team for the project Unraveling the effects of contemporary and historical changes in climate and land use on freshwater biodiversity in high-latitude regions of Europe and North America . The project is the Kvantum Institute’s spearhead project for the period of 2025-2028. Description of the position We are looking for one (1) talented and highly motivated research-oriented person to carry out postdoctoral research addressing the effects of contemporary and historical changes in climate and land use on freshwater biodiversity in high-latitude regions of Europe and North America. The project aims to answer: Is land-use intensification a stronger driver of change than changing climate in explaining historical freshwater plant diversity and distribution? Are historical legacies of past climates and land use still shaping distribution and functions of present-day freshwater flora in Europe and North America? Are there long-lasting biotic imprints affecting contemporary freshwater plant communities, and do these legacies differ between continents? The postdoctoral researcher will conduct research in the project (in a fixed two (2) year term), publish research results in reputable international journals, and contribute to developing new proposals to further research in this area. Other duties may include teaching in undergraduate courses (up to 10% of the total 1612 working hours per year) and co-supervising master's and doctoral students. Also, you will present research in the Kvantum Institute’s Researchers’ Seminar and possibly international conferences. In addition, you may have to participate in administrative tasks of the university and/or the Geography Research Unit. Description of the research team The postdoctoral researcher will join a multinational research team of biogeographers and ecologists. Dr. Janne Alahuhta (University of Oulu, Finland), MSc Misha Tseitlin (University of Oulu), Dr. Jorge Garcia-Giron (University of Leon, Spain), Dr. Daniel Larkin (University of Minnesota, USA) and Dr. Danelle Larson (US Geological Survey, USA) make up the project’s core research team. The position will be based in the Physical Geography Research Group ( PGRG ) co-led by Senior Researcher Janne Alahuhta and located at the University of Oulu, Finland. PGRG contributes to cutting-edge global change research by focusing on a wide range of complementing study questions related to abiotic and biotic earth surface systems, including also Macrophyte Biogeography Lab led by Dr. Alahuhta. Qualification requirements for the Postdoctoral researcher position PhD in Geography, Ecology, Environmental Sciences, Biostatistics, or another related discipline. The doctoral degree must have been received no more than 10 years ago. Demonstrated experience in community ecology or species distribution modelling using R. Advanced level work in R (or Python) and previous experience in functional and phylogenetic biodiversity approaches are considered an additional asset. Knowledge of aquatic ecosystems and/or aquatic plant ecology is considered a benefit. Basic expertise in GIS (e.g. ArcGIS or QGIS) is required; advanced level in GIS is preferred. Experience managing and harmonizing heterogeneous ecological, environmental, climatic, or related datasets is required. Ability for independent scientific work. Open-minded and enthusiastic towards research. Fluency in both written and spoken English. Good communication and teamwork skills. Proven track record of securing competitive research funding (e.g., national research council, foundations) is considered a strong merit. When assessing the candidate’s merits for the position of Postdoctoral Researcher, attention will be paid to scientific excellence, such as research outputs, international scientific activities and collaboration, supervision of undergraduate students, pedagogical competence, societal relevance, impact and potential of scientific activities, and services for the academic community. What we offer You will become a part of a highly talented research group that is working on strategically and globally significant research areas. The support of an experienced and enthusiastic research team where you can share and grow your expertise. Wellness benefit ePassi covering sport, culture, and well-being. Read more about other staff benefits here. Our Buddy Programme and Spouse Network support you and your close ones in settling into Oulu. Development and career options of the big organization. We have an HR Excellence in Research -quality label, which is a recognition awarded by the European Commission for the development of researchers’ working conditions and careers. Work that matters and a workplace that promotes flexibility and work-life balance. Read more about working with us. Finland is one of the most livable countries in the world, with a high quality of life, safety, an excellent education system, and a competitive economy. Read more about living in Oulu . Salary The position is fixed-term for two (2) years as of 01.01.2027 or as soon as possible thereafter. The project lasts until the end of 2028. The salary will be based on the levels 5-6 of the demand level chart for teaching and research staff of Finnish universities. In addition, a salary component based on personal work performance will be paid (a maximum of 50 % of the job-specific component). The starting gross salary will be approx. 3900-4300 € per month (before taxes). A trial period of 6 months is applied to the position. How to apply? Interested? If yes, please apply by 30.9.2026 (23:59 Finnish local time, UTC +3) through our recruitment system. The application should be written in English and include the following: A motivation letter (max. 2 pages) summarizing the applicant’s professional experience and expertise and describing why the applicant is interested in this position. Also, information on personal research interests, experience, and career plans are highly encouraged. CV , following the guidelines of the Finnish Advisory Board on Research Integrity List of publications , following the guidelines of the Research Council of Finland Contact information of two senior/experienced researchers who may be asked to give a statement on the candidate The eligible applicants fitting best in the profile expected for the position will be invited to an on-site or remote interview. The shortlisted candidates will also be asked to submit their diplomas, and their references will be contacted. All applicants will be notified during the selection process. We welcome applicants from all backgrounds, including people of different ages, genders, languages, cultures, and minority communities. Contact Information If you have any further questions, please contact Senior Researcher Janne Alahuhta, Geography Research Unit, janne.alahuhta@oulu.fi Type of employment Temporary position over 6 months Employment expires 2028-12-31 Contract type Full time First day of employment 1.1.2027 Salary TES Number of positions 1 Full-time equivalent 100% City Oulu County Pohjois-Pohjanmaa Country Finland Reference number 2026/490 Contact Janne Alahuhta, 050-3662601, janne.alahuhta@oulu.fi Published 14.Aug.2026 Last application date 30.Sep.2026 Login and apply Share links Return to job vacancies Grade Varbi Recruit recruitment system Cookies Terms Data privacy policy Accessibility statement × Modal title We use cookies for login, improved user experience, share links and in some cases marketing and collection of statistics. Accept all cookies Accept only necessary Read more about our cookies here ×"
    },
    "https://oulunyliopisto.varbi.com/en/what:job/jobID:958304/": {
      "title": "Postdoctoral Researcher, in the FRONT research programme",
      "description": "Postdoctoral Researcher, in the FRONT research programme Login and apply Swedish Norwegian Danish Finnish German Dutch Chinese (BETA) Polish French Romanian Norwegian (nynorsk) Postdoctoral Researcher, in the FRONT research programme Login and apply Faculty of Education and Psychology, Teacher education, school and society The University of Oulu is a multidisciplinary, international research university, with about 4000 employees who produce new knowledge based on high-standards research and provide research based education to build a more sustainable, smarter, and more humane world. The University of Oulu community has about 19,000 people in total. Our northern scientific community operates globally and creates conditions for the emergence of innovations. The University of Oulu is ranked in the top 3% of the world’s universities. All our research, education, and community activities are guided by our university’s values and ethical principles. We are now looking for a Postdoctoral Researcher to join us in the Frontiers of Arctic and Global Resilience (FRONT) research programme at the University of Oulu. The postdoctoral researcher position will be placed in the Faculty of Education and Psychology. The FRONT research programme forms a part of our national profiling actions supported by the Research Council of Finland. FRONT programme focuses on changing human-environment relations and challenges to cope and adapt with that change and aims to ground-breaking transdisciplinary research on resilience and how to ‘Adapt for Our Future’ in the Arctic and elsewhere on the planet. The programme involves cutting-edge research to advance the existing frontiers of knowledge on systemic changes needed for resilience planning and governance, and for finding solutions to the wicked problems of resilience across the social and environmental sciences. FRONT focuses on international top-level collaborative and transdisciplinary research on socio-economic and socio-ecological resilience in different scales across social and environmental sciences, supported by the new Resilience Academy. By bringing together international, national and University of Oulu-based scholars from across disciplines, and encouraging effective public communication of science, FRONT will promote inter- and transdisciplinary and citizen-engaged studies of the environment and raise the University’s profile as an international leader in addressing the challenges of humans in change and human impacts and dependency on environment. About the job We are looking for a postdoctoral researcher in psychology (social psychology, environmental psychology, political psychology, developmental psychology etc.), education, or a neighboring social science field. The two-year project will be exploring “critical emotional awareness (CEA)” (Ojala, 2023, 2026) as a possible resilience factor against disinformation/propaganda and for civic engagement among young people in a time of polycrisis (climate change, war etc.). The age groups in focus in the project are young people between late childhood and up to young adulthood. The preliminary plan is that the post doc in collaboration with the project leader will: (1) Conduct interviews to explore young people’s emotions, and views about emotions, in relation to different intertwined societal problems (polycrisis), analyze, write, and publish an article on the data. (2) Based on earlier research and the interviews and in collaboration with young people create a survey scale capturing CEA, test how this scale works in groups of young people and publish articles on the data. Besides working in FRONT, you will work together with colleagues in the SERSus (Socio-Ecological Resilience and Sustainability) research group, led by Prof. Maria Ojala (who is also the project leader of this post doc project), at the Faculty of Education and Psychology, University of Oulu. As a postdoctoral researcher you will also Collaborate in service to FRONT programme, faculty, and university Participate in the development and activities of the Resilience Academy of Oulu (RAO) Engage in writing and submitting applications for research funding Take part in teaching activities, subject to faculty and research unit needs and your own teaching/research capabilities and interests What we offer We offer you a supportive academic environment in a community of committed scholars and the possibility to make use of funding opportunities to generate new research ideas and build an innovative programme that will attract international scholars. The University of Oulu offers flexible working hours, an excellent work-life balance and provides a range of occupational healthcare services. Our competitive salaries include paid leave and an additional holiday bonus in the summer. The support of an experienced and enthusiastic team of people, with whom you can share your expertise and grow as an expert. Wellness benefit ePassi covering sport, culture, and well-being. Read more about other staff benefits here. Our Buddy Programme and Spouse Network support you and your close ones in settling into Oulu. Development and career options of the big organization. We have an HR Excellence in Research -quality label, which is a recognition awarded by the European Commission for the development of researchers’ working conditions and careers. Work that matters and a workplace that promotes flexibility and work-life balance. Read more about working with us. Finland is one of the most livable countries in the world, with a high quality of life, safety, an excellent education system, and a competitive economy. Read more about living in Oulu . What we expect A doctoral degree in a relevant field that was awarded not more than ten years ago Skills in advanced statistical analyses and a solid experience in working with quantitative survey studies and preferably with scale development Experience of qualitative methods in the form of conducting interviews and analyzing interview data Good, demonstrated capacity to collaborate in research and research dissemination activities Excellent written and interpersonal communication skills in English We also appreciate: Knowledge of other methodological approaches and multidisciplinary experience A transdisciplinary research orientation with demonstrated research experience or interest Earlier experience of research about emotions in a societal context Earlier experience of psychological or educational research about climate change and other sustainability issues As a person you are creative, analytical, curious, open to other scientific disciplines, and can conduct excellent research in a novel subfield. When assessing the candidate’s merits for the position of Postdoctoral Researcher, attention will also be paid to scientific excellence, such as research outputs, international scientific activities and collaboration, supervision of undergraduate students, pedagogical competence, societal relevance, impact and potential of scientific activities, and services for the academic community. Salary The position is fixed-term for two years, starting at the latest on 1st of January 2027 or as soon as possible thereafter. The salary will be based on the levels 5-6 of the demand level chart for teaching and research staff of Finnish universities. In addition, a salary component based on personal work performance will be paid (a maximum of 50 % of the job-specific component). The starting gross salary will be approx. 3700-4300 € per month (before taxes). A trial period of 6 months is applied to the position. How to apply? Interested? If yes, please apply by 30th of September 2026 (23:59 Finnish local time) through our recruitment system. The application should be written in English and include the following: Cover letter CV , following the guidelines of the Finnish Advisory Board on Research Integrity List of publications , following the guidelines of the Research Council of Finland Certificates/Diplomas: Scanned copy of the original Ph.D. degree certificate and, when necessary, official translations to Finnish or English. In case the degree is still in process, please give an official notification from the supervisor or faculty to address the estimated date of defense. Contact information of two senior/experienced researchers who may be asked to give a statement on the candidate. The eligible applicants fitting best in the profile expected for the position will be invited to an on-site or remote interview. The shortlisted candidates will also be asked to submit their diplomas, and their references will be contacted. All applicants will be notified during the selection process. We welcome applicants from all backgrounds, including people of different ages, genders, languages, cultures, and minority communities. Contact Information If you have any further questions, please contact FRONT coordinator Dr Lotta Haukipuro (lotta.haukipuro@oulu.fi) or the project leader Prof. Maria Ojala (maria.ojala@oulu.fi) Type of employment Temporary position over 6 months Contract type Full time Number of positions 1 Full-time equivalent 100% City Oulu County Pohjois-Pohjanmaa Country Finland Reference number 2026/501 Contact Lotta Haukipuro, lotta.haukipuro@oulu.fi Maria Ojala, maria.ojala@oulu.fi Published 14.Aug.2026 Last application date 30.Sep.2026 Login and apply Share links Return to job vacancies Grade Varbi Recruit recruitment system Cookies Terms Data privacy policy Accessibility statement × Modal title We use cookies for login, improved user experience, share links and in some cases marketing and collection of statistics. Accept all cookies Accept only necessary Read more about our cookies here ×"
    },
    "https://oulunyliopisto.varbi.com/en/what:job/jobID:948111/": {
      "title": "Doctoral Researcher, Multimodal AI and Physiological Sensing for Cardiometabolic Health",
      "description": "Doctoral Researcher, Multimodal AI and Physiological Sensing for Cardiometabolic Health Login and apply Swedish Norwegian Danish Finnish German Dutch Chinese (BETA) Polish French Romanian Norwegian (nynorsk) Doctoral Researcher, Multimodal AI and Physiological Sensing for Cardiometabolic Health Login and apply Faculty of Medicine, Health Sciences and Technology The University of Oulu is a multidisciplinary, international research university, with about 4000 employees who produce new knowledge based on high-standards research and provide research based education to build a more sustainable, smarter, and more humane world. The University of Oulu community has about 19,000 people in total. Our northern scientific community operates globally and creates conditions for the emergence of innovations. The University of Oulu is ranked in the top 3% of the world’s universities. All our research, education, and community activities are guided by our university’s values and ethical principles. We are now looking for a Doctoral Researcher to join a multidisciplinary research environment spanning two faculties at the University of Oulu: the Research Unit of Health Sciences and Technology (HST), Faculty of Medicine the Center for Machine Vision and Signal Analysis (CMVS), Computer Science and Engineering, Faculty of Information Technology and Electrical Engineering The position offers a distinctive opportunity to conduct research at the intersection of artificial intelligence, signal processing, computer vision, and digital health. The objective of the position is to carry out high-quality doctoral research and to complete a doctoral degree during the four-year employment period. About the job The position is part of the Research Council of Finland-funded Academy Research Fellow project led by Dr. Xiaoting Wu: CARDIAB: Towards Cardiometabolic Intelligence—Decoding Heart Dynamics for AI-Augmented Diabetes Monitoring and Human Sustainable Wellbeing . As a doctoral researcher, you will: Conduct doctoral research on multimodal physiological sensing and AI-based analysis of cardiac dynamics. Process and analyze ECG, PPG, camera-based physiological measurements, and radar signals. Contribute to the design of data collection protocols, sensor synchronization, data annotation, and research data management. Evaluate associations between multimodal physiological patterns, diabetes-related factors, and broader indicators of cardiometabolic health. Collaborate with researchers from computer science, engineering, health sciences, and medicine. Complete doctoral studies at the University of Oulu Graduate School. Publish research findings in high-quality international journals and conferences. What we offer A fully funded, full-time doctoral researcher position for four years. Joint multidisciplinary research support from the Faculty of Medicine and the Faculty of Information Technology and Electrical Engineering. Access to expertise in artificial intelligence, computer vision, physiological signal analysis, biomedical engineering, digital health, and health sciences. Access to multimodal sensing equipment, experimental facilities, research datasets, and computational resources. Opportunities for international collaboration, conference participation, and research visits when relevant to the doctoral project. Wellness benefit ePassi covering sport, culture, and well-being. Read more about other staff benefits. Development and career options of the big organization. Work that matters and a workplace that promotes flexibility and work-life balance. Read more about working with us . Our Buddy Programme and Spouse Network support you and your close ones in settling into Oulu. We have an HR Excellence in Research -quality label, which is a recognition awarded by the European Commission for the development of researchers’ working conditions and careers. Finland is one of the most livable countries in the world, with a high quality of life, safety, an excellent education system, and a competitive economy. Read more about living in Oulu. Who are you? In order to succeed and enjoy the position, we require from you: Master's degree in a relevant field, such as computer science, electronic engineering, data science, or a comparable discipline. A Master's degree must have been completed before the start of the doctoral researcher's work. Strong programming and data processing skills with C/C++/Matlab/python. Foundational knowledge of machine learning, digital signal processing, and statistical data analysis. Motivation to conduct long-term doctoral research in a multidisciplinary environment. Fluent in written and spoken English. The ability to work both independently and collaboratively. You must apply for the right to study for a doctoral degree at the beginning of your employment in accordance with the requirements of the University of Oulu Graduate School (UniOGS). We also appreciate experience in physiological or biomedical signal processing. computer vision or camera-based physiological measurements. research publications, open-source software, or previous research projects. Salary The position is full-time and a fixed term for 4 years. The employment will begin as soon as possible after the completion of the recruitment process. The salary will be based on levels 2-4 of the demand level chart for teaching and research staff of Finnish universities. In addition, a salary component based on personal work performance will be paid (a maximum of 50% of the job-specific component). The starting gross salary will be approx. 2500-3200 € per month (before taxes). A trial period of 6 months is applied to the position. How to apply? Interested? If yes, please apply by 5.9.2026 (23:59 Finnish local time) through our recruitment system. The application should be written in English and include the following: Cover letter, maximum one page. Introduce yourself and explain your motivation for applying, your interest in the research topic, and how your academic background supports the proposed doctoral research. CV following the guidelines of the Finnish Advisory Board on Research Integrity. Research plan, maximum three pages+ references , following the guidelines of the Academy of Finland. The eligible applicants fitting best in the profile expected for the position will be invited to an on-site or remote interview. The shortlisted candidates will also be asked to submit their diplomas and transcripts, and their references will be contacted. All applicants will be notified during the selection process. We welcome applicants from all backgrounds, including people of different ages, genders, languages, cultures, and minority communities. Contact Information If you have any further questions, please contact Dr. Xiaoting Wu University of Oulu Email: xiaoting.wu@oulu.fi Prof. Kristina Mikkonen University of Oulu Email: kristina.mikkonen@oulu.fi Type of employment Temporary position over 6 months Contract type Full time Number of positions 1 Full-time equivalent 100% City Oulu County Pohjois-Pohjanmaa Country Finland Reference number 2026/452 Published 13.Aug.2026 Last application date 05.Sep.2026 Login and apply Share links Return to job vacancies Grade Varbi Recruit recruitment system Cookies Terms Data privacy policy Accessibility statement × Modal title We use cookies for login, improved user experience, share links and in some cases marketing and collection of statistics. Accept all cookies Accept only necessary Read more about our cookies here ×"
    },
    "https://oulunyliopisto.varbi.com/en/what:job/jobID:957902/": {
      "title": "Doctoral Researcher, In-situ and Operando Spectroscopy and Scattering Techniques for Oxygen Evolution Reaction Mechanism Studies, Faculty of Science",
      "description": "Doctoral Researcher, In-situ and Operando Spectroscopy and Scattering Techniques for Oxygen Evolution Reaction Mechanism Studies, Faculty of Science Login and apply Swedish Norwegian Danish Finnish German Dutch Chinese (BETA) Polish French Romanian Norwegian (nynorsk) Doctoral Researcher, In-situ and Operando Spectroscopy and Scattering Techniques for Oxygen Evolution Reaction Mechanism Studies, Faculty of Science Login and apply Faculty of Science, Nano and Molecular Systems The University of Oulu is a multidisciplinary, international research university, with about 4000 employees who produce new knowledge based on high-standards research and provide research based education to build a more sustainable, smarter, and more humane world. The University of Oulu community has about 19,000 people in total. Our northern scientific community operates globally and creates conditions for the emergence of innovations. The University of Oulu is ranked in the top 3% of the world’s universities. All our research, education, and community activities are guided by our university’s values and ethical principles. We are now looking for a Doctoral Researcher in In-situ and Operando Spectroscopy and Scattering Techniques for Oxygen Evolution Reaction Mechanism Studies to join us in the Nano and Molecular Systems Research Unit at the Faculty of Science. About the job The doctoral researcher will join an interdisciplinary research project focused on understanding the reaction mechanisms of the oxygen evolution reaction (OER) using advanced in-situ and operando spectroscopy and scattering techniques. The project combines electrochemistry, materials science, spectroscopy, synchrotron radiation, and computational data analysis to reveal the structural, electronic, and chemical evolution of electrocatalysts under realistic operating conditions. The research will involve the design and development of advanced electrochemical cells compatible with laboratory- and synchrotron-based characterization techniques. The successful candidate will work closely with collaborators and participate in experimental studies at leading synchrotron radiation facilities. As a Doctoral Researcher, you will: Design, develop, and optimize in-situ and operando electrochemical cells for spectroscopy and scattering experiments. Assemble, commission, and maintain experimental setups for advanced electrochemical and spectroscopic measurements. Carry out in-situ and operando Raman spectroscopy to monitor catalyst phase evolution, surface intermediates, and reaction pathways during oxygen evolution. Perform in-situ/operando synchrotron-based experimental studies employing advanced operando characterization techniques, including X-ray absorption spectroscopy (XAS), X-ray photoelectron spectroscopy (XPS), high-energy X-ray diffraction (HEXRD), total scattering, and other complementary spectroscopy and scattering methods. Process, analyze, and interpret multimodal datasets obtained from Raman spectroscopy, XRD, XPS, XAS, and electrochemical experiments to establish structure–property–performance relationships. Develop computational workflows and automated data-processing pipelines using Python, MATLAB, and other scientific software for handling large laboratory and synchrotron datasets. Perform quantitative spectral fitting, kinetic analysis, multivariate statistical analysis, visualization, and data integration to correlate catalyst structure, oxidation state, and reaction kinetics under operating conditions. Present research findings at national/international conferences and publish results in leading peer-reviewed scientific journals. Contribute to the supervision of Bachelor's and Master's students and participate in teaching activities within the research unit. What we offer The successful candidate will receive comprehensive training in advanced operando spectroscopy and scattering techniques, electrochemistry, synchrotron radiation experiments, scientific programming, and multimodal data analysis. The project provides access to state-of-the-art laboratory instrumentation and leading international synchrotron facilities, offering opportunities to collaborate with internationally recognized researchers and contribute to cutting-edge research in sustainable energy materials. The doctoral researcher will develop expertise spanning experimental design, advanced characterization, computational data analysis, and mechanistic understanding of electrocatalytic reactions, providing an excellent foundation for a future career in academia, national laboratories, or industry. In addition, we offer: Wellness benefit ePassi covering sport, culture, and well-being. Read more about other staff benefits. Development and career options of the big organization. Work that matters and a workplace that promotes flexibility and work-life balance. Read more about working with us . Our Buddy Programme and Spouse Network support you and your close ones in settling into Oulu. We have an HR Excellence in Research -quality label, which is a recognition awarded by the European Commission for the development of researchers’ working conditions and careers. Finland is one of the most livable countries in the world, with a high quality of life, safety, an excellent education system, and a competitive economy. Read more about living in Oulu. Who are you? We expect you to have: An MSc degree in Physics, Materials Science, Chemistry, Chemical Engineering, or a closely related discipline. Strong interest in electrocatalysis, renewable energy technologies, and advanced materials characterization. Experience with one or more experimental techniques such as Raman spectroscopy, X-ray diffraction (XRD), X-ray photoelectron spectroscopy (XPS), X-ray absorption spectroscopy (XAS), electron microscopy, or electrochemical characterization is a plus. Experience with scientific programming and data analysis using Python, MATLAB, or similar programming languages. Knowledge of spectral processing, curve fitting, statistical analysis, scientific visualization, and handling large experimental datasets is considered plus. Excellent written and spoken English. Strong analytical thinking, problem-solving ability, and the capability to work both independently and as part of an international multidisciplinary research team. Willingness to travel and participate in experimental campaigns at synchrotron radiation facilities. You must apply for the right to study for a doctoral degree at the beginning of your employment in accordance with the requirements of the University of Oulu Graduate School (UniOGS). Salary The position is fixed-term for 4 years as of 1.10.2026 or as soon as possible thereafter. The salary will be based on the levels 2-4 of the demand level chart for teaching and research staff of Finnish universities. In addition, a salary component based on personal work performance will be paid (a maximum of 50 % of the job-specific component). The starting gross salary will be approx. 2600-3200 € per month (before taxes).  A trial period of 6 months is applied to the position. How to apply? Interested? If yes, please apply by 11.9.2026 (23:59 Finnish local time) through our recruitment system. The application should be written in English and include the following: Cover letter CV following the guidelines of the Finnish Advisory Board on Research Integrity Narrative CV , using the given template (more information: principles for the assessment of research and researchers at the University of Oulu ) The eligible applicants fitting best in the profile expected for the position will be invited to an on-site or remote interview. The shortlisted candidates will also be asked to submit their diplomas, and their references will be contacted. All applicants will be notified during the selection process. We welcome applicants from all backgrounds, including people of different ages, genders, languages, cultures, and minority communities. Contact Information If you have any further questions, please contact Dr. Ekta Rani, Faculty of Science, Nano and Molecular Systems Research Unit, ekta.rani@oulu.fi Dr. Samuli Urpelainen, Faculty of Science, Nano and Molecular Systems Research Unit, samuli.urpelainen@oulu.fi Type of employment Temporary position over 6 months Contract type Full time Number of positions 1 Full-time equivalent 100% City Oulu County Pohjois-Pohjanmaa Country Finland Reference number 2026/495 Published 12.Aug.2026 Last application date 11.Sep.2026 Login and apply Share links Return to job vacancies Grade Varbi Recruit recruitment system Cookies Terms Data privacy policy Accessibility statement × Modal title We use cookies for login, improved user experience, share links and in some cases marketing and collection of statistics. Accept all cookies Accept only necessary Read more about our cookies here ×"
    },
    "https://oulunyliopisto.varbi.com/what:subscribe/": {
      "title": "Työpaikkavahti",
